From 7ee7ca9e97a73dfbeb438c064c7e91fdd25db65d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:53:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Zeppelin I-442: sun contact shadows under MSAA - a depth-only
 contact pass on the resolved scene depth

- HD.SunContactDepth (AfterOpaqueWorld, order 55): runs only when MSAA blocks the G-buffer soft-shadow path and
  hdSunShadows + hdSunContact are on (1x keeps the full path; no double darkening). Port of the D3D9 HdContactShadow v4:
  24-step view-space march toward the sun against the resolved depth, thickness test, 16 character capsules (receive,
  feet cast), native shadow-map check (extended bands) to skip ground the maps already shadow; darkness 0.7 or
  ambient/(ambient+diffuse N.L) on Forever ground; depth-aware blur. hdSunContactLength/Thickness/Strength apply.
- hdSunInfo: "contact only (depth): MSAA is on (gxMultisample N) ...". Loop bounds from constants (lavapipe unrolled
  fixed bounds very slowly).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UHcJJVC4feQ4s15e9bNRoN
